{"findings":[{"issue":"Incomplete s2 repair: an unresolved approval can still receive Enter. When a parallel command has exceeded 600 seconds, refresh selects long_command ahead of a newer PermissionRequest. Claude's actual file-edit question, “Do you want to make this edit to …?”, also escapes approvalDialog. Consequently this check permits sending into the affirmative approval selection. An in-memory reproduction recorded both text and Enter reaching the pending dialog, allowing an unapproved edit outside the workspace.","file":"lib/agent.js","line":"524","quote":"  const dialog = approvalDialog(w, screen(w));\n  if (result.state === 'stuck' || dialog) {","suggestion":"Reject unresolved approval requests independently of the earliest reported fault, and recognize the harness's file-edit approval dialogs.","likelihood":3,"impact":10,"protected":true,"trigger":"A Claude worker has a parallel command open for over 600 seconds and a newer file-edit approval pending; call agent send while Yes is selected.","preExisting":false,"instances":null},{"issue":"New regression: ordinary answer text is mistaken for an approval dialog. A completed answer containing a standalone “Would you like to proceed?” matches this detector without any choices or permission hook. Reproduction returned done from wait, then exit 3 from send, preventing the follow-up while that answer remains visible.","file":"lib/agent.js","line":"264","quote":"  return index < 0 ? null : { kind: 'permission', prompt: rows.slice(index).join('\\n').trim() };","suggestion":"Require evidence of an active approval interface, including its choices, instead of matching question text alone.","likelihood":3,"impact":5,"protected":false,"trigger":"A worker finishes with a multiline answer containing “Would you like to proceed?”; send it a follow-up using agent send.","preExisting":false,"instances":null}]}
